✅ Bulkified trigger → Successful execution
7. Asynchronous Apex — @future
Objective

Create a simple @future method that:

Accepts a record Id
Queries the record
Updates one field
Executes asynchronously

The PDF requires checking Setup → Apex Jobs afterward to confirm that the asynchronous job ran.

Apex Class
public class MemberFutureService {

    @future
    public static void updateMember(Id memberId) {

        Member__c member = [
            SELECT Id, Name
            FROM Member__c
            WHERE Id = :memberId
            LIMIT 1
        ];

        member.Name = member.Name + ' Updated';

        update member;
    }
}
Execute Anonymous

Use an actual Member Id from your org:

Member__c member = [
    SELECT Id
    FROM Member__c
    LIMIT 1
];

MemberFutureService.updateMember(member.Id);
Verify

Go to:

Setup → Apex Jobs

You should see the asynchronous job there.

