10. LWC — Child to Parent Communication

The second requirement is the opposite direction:

Child
  ↓
Custom Event
  ↓
Parent
  ↓
Updates screen

The PDF specifically asks for a button in the child that fires a custom event, with the parent listening and updating something on screen.

Child JS
import { LightningElement, api } from 'lwc';

export default class MemberChild extends LightningElement {

    @api recordId;

    handleClick() {

        const event = new CustomEvent('memberupdate', {
            detail: {
                message: 'Child button was clicked'
            }
        });

        this.dispatchEvent(event);
    }
}
Child HTML
<template>

    <lightning-card title="Child Component">

        <lightning-button
            label="Send Message"
            onclick={handleClick}>
        </lightning-button>

    </lightning-card>

</template>
Parent HTML
<template>

    <lightning-card title="Parent Component">

        <c-member-child
            record-id={memberId}
            onmemberupdate={handleMemberUpdate}>
        </c-member-child>

        <p>{message}</p>

    </lightning-card>

</template>
Parent JS
import { LightningElement } from 'lwc';

export default class MemberParent extends LightningElement {

    memberId = 'YOUR_MEMBER_RECORD_ID';

    message = 'Waiting for child...';

    handleMemberUpdate(event) {

        this.message = event.detail.message;

    }
}
